Okay, I need to figure out this problem where I have n barrels, each with k staves (so total m=nk staves), and I need to partition all these staves into exactly n barrels where each barrel has exactly k staves. Each barrel must have minimal length (volume vj) and I need to maximize the total sum such that every pair of different barrels doesn't differ in volume by more than l. If impossible to do that, output 0. Hmm.

Let me think through this step by step. 

First, I need to split all staves into n groups of k staves each, making sure that the minimal length in each group is as large as possible while keeping each group's minimal volume from differing from others by no more than l. Also, each group has exactly one such minimal volume, since each group is considered. Wait, no. Wait: Each group is a group of k staves. The minimal length in that group contributes to its own volume, and since every group must have minimal length, so each group must have at least some value that's the minimal of that group. Also, between all groups, when comparing any two, their minimal lengths must not differ by more than l.

